WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:08.270
It's time for the fall of Hiroshima's false chivalry!

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.240
Setup complete. Idling.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.990
What's wrong? Why won't it move?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.950
Please insert the daimon coat of arms. Please insert the—

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.180
Let's save that girl, Shigyo.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.560
Us? We're just normal people right now!

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.520
There are stones in that ship.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.560
Let's go.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:52.780
You were planning on stealing back the whole ship from the start, weren't you?

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:59.760
The Future is in Our Hands

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.100
Who's that pretty lady?

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.530
The president of Tokorozawa...

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.070
Chi's mom!

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.700
I thought you were told to wait at Momiji Island?

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.200
Well, one thing led to another, and...

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.670
You heard from Momiyama?

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:33.080
Yeah.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.590
I was looking for a chance to tell you myself.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.760
I had a feeling

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.840
that I'd be leaving one day...

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.350
We'll depart from here, instead of going back to Tokorozawa.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.980
Come. We'll wait for the ship at Momiji Island.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.350
Thanks for all you've done for her.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:56.610
Excuse me!

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.230
We're in a hurry right now!

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:01.320
We were asked to deliver something.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.700
Where to?

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:04.990
Um...

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.370
To the lady at the checkpoint!

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:08.490
Huh?

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.960
It's not dangerous! We'll be right back!

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.000
Nonsuke, let's go.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.500
Wait a minute.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.340
All right.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.720
Be careful.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.270
She wasn't allowed to go out?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.770
Her mom was worried about her health.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.150
She's never even been to school.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.400
On the rare occasions when she did go outside, she had to wear a mask,

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.110
but it looks like the fears were groundless.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.280
Had we known, we would've let her go sooner.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:54.120
Can I give this to her?

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.210
Oh, sure, but let me fix it fir—

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.250
This is fine.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.250
It's a very nice picture.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.430
Hm?

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:10.430
No, it's nothing. It's the first time anyone's said that...

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.060
Thank you... very much.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.810
The callus on your drawing hand is still very small.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:24.440
People who achieve their dreams are the ones who don't give up.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.820
Our band was like that too.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.660
We were all pretty useless at first,

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.660
kind of like you girls.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.540
When people gather, a strange power is born.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.670
It was a good time.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.850
This is the end!

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.390
What? What happened?

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.020
It's a surprise attack!

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.360
The evil Takumis and Takumi-za are invading!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.560
Really?!

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.030
Takumi-za too?!

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:12.530
They must have decided to work together to retrieve their shrine.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.540
We'll show them! Hit 'em with all we've got!

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.700
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:17.250
How many?

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:17.870
Answer her.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:18.370
What now?

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:19.540
Less talking, more moving!

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:22.880
Th-They're everywhere!

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.010
They're coming up here, too!

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.270
Hey, you guys!

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.190
Leave them.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:40.900
But...

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.070
It's the same as before.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.400
No, they're abandoning me even sooner this time.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.410
I'll head out in the Stonefish. You protect the shrine.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.330
Miss Shima! Should we return that?

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.410
If we crush everything, then no one else can buy their automatons.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.290
That would be better for us.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:04:59.870
But—

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.920
Weren't you going to stay by my side, Otomo?!

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.590
This whole place is a laboratory.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:12.640
There are spectators watching to see how far the human ego can go

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.390
by giving them simple rules.

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:16.060
A laboratory?

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:20.230
End it all. Drag them out and crush them!

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.980
That's what this ship was for.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.270
You're delusional!

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:28.990
The Twin Tower Declaration is the last system in place to keep people from destroying themselves with war!

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:31.490
The little, happy things in life form the foundation of pea—

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:34.740
Then why are the Takumi-za and evil Takumis allowed to exist?

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.920
We're being tested to see how we'll use them.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.120
That's right. By them—

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:48.130
By the age we live in. That doesn't change, no matter the time or the planet.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:50.170
Planet?

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:51.050
Huh?

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.640
Ishizukuri Shima.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:58.470
Return what you stole from Takumi-za and the evil Takumis.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.640
It's not the same as before...

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:08.020
Even if everyone else ran away,
you still have someone by your side.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:10.320
That's why I can't return it!

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.150
Why not?!

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:12.400
License

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:12.530
License

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:12.650
License

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:12.950
License

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:13.400
License

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:13.530
License

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:13.660
License

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:14.780
License

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.910
You can have the license back. Forget the ship.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:14.910
License

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:15.030
License

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:15.160
License

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:15.280
License

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:15.410
License

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:16.910
License

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.160
Now, leave!

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:48.940
Is that the Takumi-za sacred object?

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.240
You may want to return that graciously.

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.240
Unfortunately, I am not allowed to.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.830
Carry that outside and wave a white flag!

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.790
If you do, this attack will stop.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.840
B-But I... I'll get—

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.420
"If you keep going, you'll reach your destination!

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.470
For now, just run!"

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:15.930
The chorus of "Song of the Beginning"!

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.430
Go!

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.180
Yes, sir!

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.930
One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.890
Did she snap?

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.690
That woman is dumber than I thought.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:08.560
We have to stop her.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.570
You're not stopping anyone in that condition.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.570
One, two!

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:23.160
It's not an exit!

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.410
Let's go back!

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.460
Otonashi?

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:47.560
Otonashi!

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.480
Otonashi!

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:58.690
Madam Shigyo?

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.110
Are you all right?

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:01.200
Madam Shigyo!

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.330
I've missed you!

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:07.500
Huh? What?

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:09.080
Huh?

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.250
Huh?

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.170
Huh?

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:20.510
Th-That stone

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.470
had nothing to do with it!

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:38.610
Again, please insert the daimon coat of arms. Please insert...

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:43.030
What is this place?

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:44.120
It's so big!

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.120
The robot!

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:47.540
Nozomi!

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.490
Masami?

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:49.830
Oh, Yukippe!

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:49.830
Yukina?!

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.120
You're okay?

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:55.500
Kaguya!

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:01.510
He said to put this in the robot!

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.650
Nozomi!

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:21.280
Nozomi are you—

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:21.280
Oh no!

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:23.240
Look for pieces of the coat of arms!

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.570
Oh, Yukina, around there!

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:28.580
Um, where?

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.620
A piece flew over there, too!

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.340
Chiaya...

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:47.390
Got it!

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:49.100
She got it!

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:08.910
Kaguya, this is from Mr. Kuramochi!

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.410
He said it's the soul of the Nayotake!

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.660
Kuramochi...

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:17.420
I think you need to insert it there.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.420
Daimon, complete.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:23.460
You can do it!

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:30.430
Nozomi...

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:31.180
Masami!

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.640
Are your injuries okay, now?

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.600
Yeah. What about you?

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.100
I'm fine.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.400
Because I'm with everyone.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:46.150
Masami!

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:47.570
Let's go!

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:48.240
Otonashi.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:50.580
Take care of those pieces.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.620
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:55.120
We'll stop Ishizukuri Shima.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:58.540
You guys use that to stop Takumi-za and the evil Takumis.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.540
Okay.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.050
I'm counting on you, Nozomi.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:07.170
Okay!

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.890
The chivalrous robot, Daimon,
will protect honor and humanity!

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:19.350
I think I can finally become a superhero.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:24.900
Let's sing a never-ending song for the bastards of the world

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.480
Madam Shigyo!

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.190
Are those two friends now?

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:30.200
Let's sing a never-ending song for the scum of the world

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:35.450
Let's sing a never-ending song for you, me, and all of them

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:35.200
In the end, what I wanted was...

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:40.710
Let's sing a never-ending song so we can laugh tomorrow

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:51.300
I don't like collusion, so it's not my fault if I'm misunderstood

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:56.350
Even so, I think about you all the time

00:12:56.350 --> 00:13:01.560
Let's sing a never-ending song for the bastards of the world

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:06.730
Let's sing a never-ending song for the scum of the world

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.770
Kaguya?

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:08.820
I'm not letting you fall to ruin without ever living a proper life!

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:11.950
Let's sing a never-ending song for you, me, and all of them

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.570
Leave that ship to us!

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:17.620
Let's sing a never-ending song so we can laugh tomorrow

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.910
Who are those two, anyway?

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:33.640
Let's sing a never-ending song for the bastards of the world

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:38.970
Let's sing a never-ending song for the scum of the world

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:44.400
Let's sing a never-ending song on the nights we cry alone

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:49.570
Let's sing a never-ending song on the days we're treated like

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.200
Hey!

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:54.660
Let's sing a never-ending song for the bastards of the world

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:56.740
Hey!

00:13:54.660 --> 00:14:00.000
Let's sing a never-ending song for you, me, and all of them

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.960
Let's sing a never-ending song so we can laugh tomorrow

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:17.140
Who ran through all that gunfire to deliver the Nayotake coat of arms?

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.600
Couldn't possibly have been the old man, could it?

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:22.310
It was Nozomi and her friends.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:23.440
Nozomi?

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:27.110
The girl that tried to stop me before.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:30.820
Oh, that little shrimp.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:35.360
They're like the Tanashi Tower, huh?

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:37.240
Tanashi Tower?

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.330
During the Great Tokyo War,

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:43.870
it was the robot that secretly supported the Tokyo Tower Robot's legs.

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:48.690
Oh, right. Tell Otomo this:

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.300
"There's no need for pity."

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:15.530
Oof...

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.660
Ow...

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.790
Are you okay, Nozomi?

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:24.750
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:28.130
I wonder what the time she spent with those girls was like.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:30.130
I'm sure it was a good experience.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.670
President!

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.960
Don't slack off. You should help, too!

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:35.970
Who do you think we're doing this for?

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:37.720
Let me rest a bit.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:40.510
Anyway, you guys went too wild inside.

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:42.430
I told you I was going to use this ship, didn't I?

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:45.770
We couldn't help it. The other guys were really strong!

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.690
Hey, you two! Don't fight!

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:02.910
The one directing them is the man who formed Takumi-za.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:04.450
He formed them?

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:05.750
What do you mean?

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:10.040
You should ask him yourself.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:13.960
I have something else to attend to, so I will return to Tokorozawa.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:15.710
Momiyama!

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:20.220
Thank you.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:21.680
Don't worry about it.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:29.600
Um...

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:30.980
No, I'm not.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:31.610
Huh?

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.650
I'm sorry, but there's no time.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:37.650
If we cannot use the space-time selector, then we cannot return to our original time over there.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:42.120
We can't increase our altitude with the current output because of the influence

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:41.820
Aren't you from the Ishizukuri Stones?

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.660
of the Hasegawa particles disseminated as a greenhouse gas canceler.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:49.250
In addition, in order to be sure to get out of the Moon Hall, even if we have to do a rush job,

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.000
Mr. Otomo... right?

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:51.500
we must install hyper boosters on the octopus pot engines—

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:51.500
Professor?

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:56.050
Didn't you escape in the pod?

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:58.550
It came back.

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:02.140
However, I was sent far into the past.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:07.890
I put myself to sleep to await tonight's full moon, but I made a small mistake.

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:14.270
I'm so glad to see you again...

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.990
Owowowow!

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:30.750
Huh?

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:35.500
Wait, so you came to the Hiyoshicho Propellers back then for 100 yen?

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:36.500
Yes.

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:42.260
I was fine just buying it for her,

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:45.550
but then I figured I needed every yen when traveling.

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:47.720
I think you said it took you three days to find us.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.520
Didn't the gas money end up being more?

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:55.730
But because of that, I was able to travel with everyone.

00:17:55.730 --> 00:17:58.690
I was also able to resolve my undecided heart.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:04.660
Chi said she was definitely not going to sleep tonight.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:06.490
She must've been tired.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.620
It's so dangerous being Chi.

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:14.540
I can't believe she accidentally stowed away on a space ship.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.800
But it's just like her, isn't it?

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:20.970
She just loves suspicious laboratories.

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:26.850
Speaking of aliens, I met one before when I was little.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:29.010
Really? I played with one before, too!

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:33.190
Me, too! I feel like it could've been a dream, though...

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:35.520
Oh, yeah. I know how you feel.

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:38.980
But now that I know they exist, it's unexpectedly...

00:18:38.980 --> 00:18:41.690
You're gong home already?

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:45.110
I wonder what she's dreaming about.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:47.950
She's the one going home, though.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:49.700
Bye-bye...

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.670
Oh yeah, Chi's camera!

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:57.710
You know, the one that lets you see dreams!

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:01.340
The final checks are done.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:03.800
We will depart immediately.

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:16.850
Take care of yourself, Chi.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:19.060
You too, Uu.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:20.980
Don't get sick.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:24.190
You too, Yukippe. Thanks for the drawing.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:29.070
Nonsuke.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.030
Huh?

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:34.310
Nonsuke, you were my Maccha Green, you know?

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:43.550
But I didn't fulfill your request.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.920
No,

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.090
you fulfilled a lot of my wishes.

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:49.340
Huh?

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:54.730
Thanks, Nonsuke, Yukippe, Uu.

00:19:56.190 --> 00:19:58.190
I'll never forget you.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:10.320
Chi...

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.690
Nozomi! Nozomi!

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:44.480
Jeez, I was so worried! Auntie, I found Nonsuke!

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:45.730
Hey, Uu!

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:47.820
Just how far did you go to look for the ball?

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:50.240
Didn't I say not to wander off, Yukippe?

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:57.330
Bye-bye...

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:37.790
The stones rain down in many different eras.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:43.880
Those who draw the stones to them do not realize it is their passion that makes them fall.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:52.010
No matter the time, the era, or the planet,

00:21:52.630 --> 00:21:56.850
those caught up in rolling along live their lives, one way or another.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:01.350
People call that radiance...

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:04.150
"tomorrow"!

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:29.760
Thou shalt not pass

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:35.260
Laws, reason, nobody is getting past

00:22:35.300 --> 00:22:40.810
I don't care what you say

00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:46.270
I'm not letting friends and lovers in either

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:50.400
My only companion

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:56.160
is the faint moonlight

00:22:57.240 --> 00:23:08.340
I'm now sitting in the cockpit

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:14.340
of the black shadow

00:23:14.340 --> 00:23:17.970
deep in the white moon

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:38.490
Can I keep walking straight like this?

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:44.080
I might fall into the lake

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:49.420
Even if I try asking someone for advice,

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:54.710
The path we follow won't change

00:23:55.630 --> 00:23:59.050
My only companion

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:04.690
is the faint moonlight

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:10.520
My only companion

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:15.610
is the faint moonlight

00:24:27.540 --> 00:24:33.880
You've probably already realized, but this show is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to real people, groups, or laws is coincidental.
